WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.350
- Elon Musk owns Twitter,

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.930
and now Twitter is owning Elon Musk.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.630
His first few weeks of
ownership have been interesting.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.030
And wouldn't you know it when
you light 44 billion dollars

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.440
on fire for the lulls?

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.273
You're bound to run

00:00:11.273 --> 00:00:12.630
into some legal headaches.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.890
Now things are changing so fast

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.210
that by the time you watch this video

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.350
the platform could be gone.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.870
It could be borrowed by Mark Zuckerberg.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.210
It could be turned into an NFT, I guess

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.910
or doing business as usual, who knows?

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.110
But here's a quick rundown

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.270
of everything that Musk
has accomplished so far.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.490
He fired half of Twitter's total workforce

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.400
and then scrambled to hire
some of them back after stating

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.230
that Twitter should be
politically neutral.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.640
He endorsed the Republican Party

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.250
before the midterms, I bet
that quickly backfired.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.170
He announced a new rule
requiring users engage

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.970
in parody to include parody in their bio.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.280
And then when that
didn't work to include it

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.480
in their Twitter name, which is exactly

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.220
the same thing that the
Onion just demolished

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.550
as being contradictory to
the entire point of parody.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.770
He promised advertisers that
Twitter would not become a free

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.236
for all hell scape and then loosened up

00:00:55.236 --> 00:00:57.060
on content moderation, resulting
in a measurable increase

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.790
in people being awful racist
or homophobic and leading

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.490
to a whole bunch of advertisers
leaving the platform

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.620
at least temporarily. He
got rid of the Blue Check

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.780
verification system and
replaced it with an $8 a month

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.240
subscription service that
didn't verify user identity

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.100
allowing people to impersonate
brands and celebrities.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.630
That's how we got a seemingly verified

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.867
George W. Bush tweeting,

00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:15.270
"I miss killing Iraqis."

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.560
And a seemingly verified

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.720
Rudy Giuliani saying, "Nancy Pelosi

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.670
and I do not agree on many
things, but them thangs

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.039
thanging I'll tell you what."

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:26.206
(audience applauding)

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.937
Now, all this has been great
fun to observe, but now

00:01:28.937 --> 00:01:32.460
that Twitter is a raging dumpster
fire, Musk has to contend

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.110
with some serious legal issues

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.240
including how he was forced to buy Twitter

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.750
in the first place, the FTC
gauntlet that is facing Twitter

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.910
and then there's the
wrongful termination suits

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.320
and possible bankruptcy.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.240
It's a real Sue's sue.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.340
Now, when we last visited
Elon Musk and Twitter,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.320
Musk was arguing that
Twitter had misled him

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.910
about the number of bots on Twitter

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.790
and that it's now former
leadership had fired employees

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:54.630
without his consent.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.340
So he was calling off the deal.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.173
At the time

00:01:57.173 --> 00:01:58.890
I speculated that it would
be tough for him to get

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.660
out of that deal to buy the company,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.063
take it from Devon from the past.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.360
Delaware courts have been known to

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.450
order specific performance
in just such a situation

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.830
as this.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:11.663
Twitter sued Musk

00:02:11.663 --> 00:02:14.370
for a specific performance in
the Delaware Chancery Court.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.440
They wanted to force
him to purchase Twitter

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.820
at the agreed upon price.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.410
The Chancery Court has jurisdiction to

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.300
hear all matters related
to equity, which means

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.520
that it had the power to compel him to go

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.630
through with a purchase.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.180
Musk wanted a discovery
process that would take months

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.410
if not years to complete.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.300
But in July, the court ruled that Musk

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.910
and Twitter needed to be
ready for trial by October.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.430
That's an insanely fast
timeline for a major trial

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.130
but such is life in the
Delaware Transfer Court.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.740
They do not mess around presumably feeling

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.050
that he did not have enough
time to make a decent case

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.000
or just saw the writing on the wall.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.760
Musk went through with the
purchase and bought the company

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.950
at the original sales
price of 44 billion dollars

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.330
on October 28th.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.210
So in the end, it was
much a sue about nothing.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.190
Now, Musk fans, what are they?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:59.400
Muskavites, I guess rejoiced
because he promised them

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.410
that he would be a
champion of free speech.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.410
Musk had assured us that
Twitter is the new town square

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.180
and everyone has a First Amendment right

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.760
to more or less say whatever
they want on the platform.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.250
Though he did begin to
backtrack almost immediately

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.110
as Musk said, by free speech

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:15.000
I simply mean that which matches the law.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.850
I'm against censorship that
goes far beyond the law.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.990
Though Musk's actions

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.210
didn't match his words almost immediately.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.130
When Twitter users
started making fun of him

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.600
he suspended their accounts.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.610
Kathy Griffin probably has an entire mug

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.960
of billionaire tears by now.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.790
And sure Musk has a legal right to

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.800
be a delicate sensitive boy.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.200
It just doesn't match
his particular rhetoric.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.970
The First Amendment prohibits
the United States government

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.220
from censoring speech,
but private companies

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.010
or private individuals can
censor speech if they want to.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.650
If Musk wants to shut down
speech from progressives

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.050
and liberals and promote
speech from conservative voices

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.660
he has a right to do that or vice versa.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.480
He can ban people who hurt his feelings

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.610
and he can turn Twitter into a hell scape

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.590
of bullying and racism
if he wants to do that.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.060
That much is obvious.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.490
However, that choice is
not without consequences.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:02.550
And Musk got a lesson in the
free market almost immediately.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.790
At least 50% of Twitter's
advertisers have fled the platform

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:06.990
since Musk took over.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:07.823
And just

00:04:07.823 --> 00:04:10.830
as Musk has a right to run
Twitter the way that he wants

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.090
more or less

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.390
advertisers are free to not
advertise on the platform.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.310
That's the free market at work there.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.500
Now the issue here is that Musk claims to

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.660
be a free speech absolutist.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.370
He apparently believes
not just in free speech

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.440
in the sense that the
government can't censor people

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.080
but also consequence free speech

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.910
and that's just not how things work.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.960
And we know this in particular

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:34.140
because Elon Musk keeps
firing Twitter employees who

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.580
either make fun of Elon

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.370
or say things that Elon
doesn't agree with.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.650
Now he can do that subject

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.540
to some limitations we'll talk about later

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.980
but we can also make fun

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.110
of him for his free speech hypocrisy.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:47.010
Now, at the same time

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.080
Musk temporarily ditched a verification

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.300
in favor of a pay per blue policy

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.640
and one of the consequences
from that was that

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.430
an Eli Lilly impersonator
promised to make insulin free.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.110
And some have speculated this might have

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.810
cost the company around 15
billion dollars in market share.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.240
Though I'm skeptical
of the causation there.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.450
But still, this deters companies
from even wanting to engage

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.150
on Twitter, let alone pay the
company to run advertisements.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.250
Now, Musk says he's
going to create a content

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.620
moderation council to
review suspended accounts

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.110
but he also has fired
the entire Twitter safety

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:16.943
and security team

00:05:16.943 --> 00:05:19.350
so he'll have to build
that council from scratch.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.820
Now, Musk also fired 80%

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.380
of Twitter's contractors around the world

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.540
which maintain the core
infrastructure services

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.620
that keep the site up and running.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.810
That's probably not important.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.160
And as much as Musk would
like to believe that

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.910
the advertiser problem is
caused by activist woke brands

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.310
it might have just as much
to do with instability

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.010
and potentially a
deteriorating site experience

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.510
which might only get worse.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.343
And a day after the

00:05:40.343 --> 00:05:42.637
mass termination Musk confirmed
the dumpster fire tweeting,

00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:43.860
"By the way, I'd like to apologize

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:44.970
for Twitter being super slow

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.040
in many countries, app is doing more

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.920
than 1000 poorly bashed RPCs just

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.660
to render a home timeline."

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.280
And independent reports also state

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.600
that Twitter's code-based suffers

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.150
from sinus sotal delineation,
which could be fixed

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:59.310
with the proper flex
capacitors and proton packs.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.170
Now, it's been fun
watching Elon just tweet

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.150
through all of this, but
in all the excitement

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.130
he seems to have overlooked
a big legal issue

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.780
which is Twitter's consent decree

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.760
with the Federal Trade Commission.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.370
Twitter's chief Privacy Officer,
chief Compliance Officer

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.430
and Chief Information Security
Officer abruptly quit shortly

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.590
after Elon rolled out new product features

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.500
without the security reviews
that the FTC required

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.260
in its decree with the company,
the employees went on Slack

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.570
and warned their colleagues
that Musk's new plans

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.180
are extremely dangerous for our users.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.010
Also, given the FTC can

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:31.620
and will find Twitter
billions of dollars pursuing

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.860
to the FTC consent order
extremely detrimental

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.930
to Twitter's longevity as a platform.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.390
And the employees then posted
a link to Whistleblower Aid

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.330
a nonprofit law firm that helps
employees report corporate

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.950
or government wrongdoing.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.840
Now, what caused Musk's privacy

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.360
and security officers to
issue such a dire warning?

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:49.920
Well, it started with a consent decree

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.480
and the government agency responsible

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:54.000
for consumer protection, the
Federal Trade Commission.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.980
It all goes back to
2009 when Twitter's lack

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.260
security processes allowed hackers to

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.570
obtain unauthorized
administrative control of Twitter

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:01.890
including both access

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.100
to non-public user information
and private tweets.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.570
Hackers were also able to send

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.730
out phony tweets from any account.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.700
In 2010 the FTC sued Twitter
for misleading consumers

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.740
about the privacy of
their personal information

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.320
and for failing to protect
user phone numbers.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.190
In 2011, Twitter entered into
a consent decree with the FTC.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.620
A consent decree is an
agreement that settles a dispute

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.080
without the defendant
admitting guilt or liability.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.000
The consent decree has to be approved

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.640
by a judge making it
enforceable by the court.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:32.070
So the Twitter consent
decree barred the company

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:33.480
from making misleading statements

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.120
about the extent to which it
protects the security, privacy

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.700
and confidentiality of
non-public consumer information.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:41.040
And under the terms of the
decree, Twitter agreed to

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:42.810
maintain a comprehensive
information security

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.760
program and allow an
independent auditor to

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.380
assess its programs every other year

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.630
for the first 10 years after the decree.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.820
In May of 2022, just

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.490
as Musk was purchasing
Twitter, the FTC accused

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.890
the company violating the
original consent decree.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.930
According to the FTC complaint, more

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:01.170
than 140 million Twitter
users provided email addresses

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.000
or telephone numbers to Twitter based

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.560
on Twitter's deceptive statements

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.150
that their information would be used

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.390
for specific purposes
related to account security.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.220
In reality, Twitter is accused

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.460
of using the personal data to
target users with advertising.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.010
Twitter settled this
claim paid 140 million

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.890
in fines and entered into
a new consent decree.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.080
The terms of the updated
consent decree require

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.810
significantly more stringent
monitoring of Twitter's privacy

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:28.290
and security claims, which
are audited by a third party.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.600
Twitter agreed to conduct
a privacy assessment

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.160
of any new products it launches

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.500
and provide the assessment to the FTC.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.340
Rihanna

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.350
who used to be Twitter's outside counsel

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.427
summarized Twitter's
obligations like this quote,

00:08:39.427 --> 00:08:41.190
"If Twitter so much as sneezes,

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.500
it has to do with privacy
review beforehand."

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.260
Now, we don't know if and
to what extent Twitter is

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.720
violating the FTC consent
decree, but we do know

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.910
that Elon Musk has a
history of not particularly

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:54.240
carrying what government
agencies tell him to do.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.420
So it's not clear if Twitter's new

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.140
or old staff are in compliance
with the consent decree

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.350
but more on that will
probably come out eventually.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.520
And while all of this is going on

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.290
Elon Musk put the stand on Wednesday

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.600
in the shareholder's derivative suit that

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.420
seeks to nullify the 2018
pay package that he received

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.860
as Tesla's CEO.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.180
Under the terms of that deal

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.220
Musk's compensation would be divided

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.470
into 12 batches of stock
that would be dispersed

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:22.560
as Musk hit predetermined
milestones, which he did.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.230
As a result, Musk received
over 50 billion dollars

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.400
in Tesla's stock.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.440
Now, these are difficult cases to win.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.020
Generally courts don't like to
review the business decisions

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.070
of a company.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.230
This class action argues
that Tesla's board

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.150
of directors were unduly
influenced by Musk

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.800
and failed to disclose crucial information

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.770
about the deal to the shareholders
who approved the deal.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.420
But Musk had to testify in that case.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:44.820
And because he's a
legal genius, he implied

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.220
that he doesn't need to
comply with consent decrees

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:49.890
in reference to an SEC consent
decree, Musk apparently

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:52.680
said, "The consent decree
was made under duress."

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:55.350
An agreement made under duress
is not valid as a foundation

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:56.917
of law, to which he was asked,

00:09:56.917 --> 00:09:58.170
"Are you trained as a lawyer?"

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.167
To which he replied,

00:09:59.167 --> 00:10:01.260
"I have some familiarity
with the legal system.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.640
If you're in enough lawsuits

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.350
you pick up a few things along the way."

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.690
The thing is, the FTC doesn't mess around.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:10.410
Many have argued that the
SEC doesn't have enough teeth

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.210
but the FTC sometimes in conjunction

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.760
with the DOJ can make things hurt not only

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:17.190
with much bigger fines,
but sometimes jail.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.410
Just ask Uber's former
chief security officer

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.150
who was recently convicted
on federal charges

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:24.180
for obstruction against the
FTC or ask Facebook who got hit

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.230
with a 5 billion dollar

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.240
fine for violating a
consent decree related

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.260
to Cambridge Analytica.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.960
And following on the heels
of these mass firings

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.180
Elon apparently sent
another late night email

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.580
in which he told Twitter
that they needed to

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.940
be more hardcore, that
they needed to respond,

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:42.330
they were willing to put
in grueling hours or not

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:44.820
and they had until 5:00 PM to respond

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.700
or they would be fired with
three months of severance.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.250
Now, given the added debt that Musk added

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.630
to Twitter, Musk claims

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.430
that he needs to make
things profitable Twitter

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:55.530
which is why he laid off
half of Twitter's staff.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.970
And meanwhile, allegedly a lawyer

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:58.440
on Twitter's privacy team has apparently

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.230
overheard Musk's lawyer say
that, "Elon is willing to take

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:02.940
on a huge amount of risk in retaliation

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:05.910
to this company and users
because Elon puts rockets

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:08.100
into space and he's
not afraid of the FTC."

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.143
And also the whistle
blowing lawyer also said

00:11:10.143 --> 00:11:12.810
that Twitter engineers would
have to take on the burden

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.850
of personally certifying that
the products they designed

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.860
for Twitter comply with
the consent decree.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.040
Now, this is obviously hearsay,
but it may also be true

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.590
because there haven't exactly
been some vociferous denials

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:23.423
of it either.

00:11:23.423 --> 00:11:24.810
Now, if true, then Twitter is requiring

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:25.643
the engineers to take

00:11:25.643 --> 00:11:28.080
on all the risk, but the
consent decree does not

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.660
allow individual employees
to certify Twitter's privacy

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.950
and security systems.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.600
The FTC agreement requires Twitter to

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.880
submit any significant
change in operations

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.490
to an outside auditor before
it can be implemented.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.200
And according to the Washington Post

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.710
the FTC expects Twitter to
submit a new audit in January.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:44.550
The sources said that

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.980
before Musk even took over,
the company was already

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:49.410
scrambling to hire enough
people to meet that deadline.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.037
And the FTC issued a statement,

00:11:51.037 --> 00:11:52.260
"When you're tracking recent developments

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:54.540
of Twitter with deep
concern, no CEO or companies

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.480
above the law and companies
must follow our consent decrees.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.820
Our revised consent order
gives us new tools to

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.220
ensure compliance and we
are prepared to use them."

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.390
And that takes us to labor

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:05.130
and employment law because
there have been lots

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:07.140
of changes for Twitter employees.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.600
Musk has fired almost
4,000 Twitter workers.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.940
And although Musk has the
right to fire employees

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.440
this right is not unlimited.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.030
Twitter still has to follow federal, state

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.230
and local laws.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:17.820
With the Federal Worker's Adjustment

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:20.010
and retraining notification
Act, also known

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:23.370
as the Warren Act, that
generally requires businesses

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.310
with 100 or more employees
to provide 60 days notice

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.350
before engaging in mass layoffs.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:30.420
Warren defines layoffs
as those affecting at

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:32.910
least 500 employees
during a 30 day period.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.070
Though employers can
provide workers with 60 days

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.920
of severance pay in lieu of
giving notice and terminated

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.750
California employees
have already filed suit

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.150
under the Warren Act in
comparable state laws.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.340
Although Musk has several
defenses to their claims,

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.410
he claims that he offered
to pay some employees

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.540
through January 4th, 2023

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.300
which could constitute
compliance with a 60 day rule.

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.190
Some employees were
offered severance package

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.110
but we don't know enough of
the details yet to determine

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:56.820
whether the packages
complied with the law.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:57.810
And Musk can also say

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.940
that the employees were fired for cause

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.640
which was his defense in a
similar lawsuit against Tesla.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.940
